  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 9,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.137,
            0.046,
            0.347,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 8"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.087,
            0.847,
            0.125
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "linked proportionally, out of which three are known and we must find the fourth, unknown, quantity."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.125,
            0.848,
            0.163
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "To solve such problems, we can model two proportional ratios using algebraic notation as"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.442,
            0.162,
            0.556,
            0.181
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_9_equation_3.jpg",
          "content": "a : b : : c : d ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.186,
            0.848,
            0.243
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "For these two ratios to be proportional, we know that term c should be a multiple of term a by a factor, say "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "f ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and term d should be a multiple of term b by the same factor f. So,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.43,
            0.246,
            0.568,
            0.291
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_9_equation_5.jpg",
          "content": "\\begin{aligned}c &= f a \\quad \\ldots (1) \\\\d &= f b \\quad \\ldots (2)\\end{aligned}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.294,
            0.503,
            0.315
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "From (1) and (2), we can say that,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.414,
            0.316,
            0.58,
            0.351
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_9_equation_7.jpg",
          "content": "f = \\frac{c}{a}  and  f = \\frac{d}{b}."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.413,
            0.353,
            0.583,
            0.386
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_9_equation_8.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{Therefore}, \\frac{c}{a} = \\frac{d}{b}."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.39,
            0.533,
            0.411
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Multiplying both sides by ab, we get,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.433,
            0.414,
            0.593,
            0.447
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_9_equation_10.jpg",
          "content": "ab \\times \\frac{c}{a} = ab \\times \\frac{d}{b}"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.431,
            0.449,
            0.592,
            0.484
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_9_equation_11.jpg",
          "content": "ab \\times \\frac{c}{a} = ab \\times \\frac{d}{b}"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.423,
            0.486,
            0.6,
            0.506
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_9_equation_12.jpg",
          "content": "b\\bar{c} = ad\\  or\\ ad = bc"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.508,
            0.848,
            0.545
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, when a : b :: c : d, then ad = bc. This is known as cross multiplication of terms."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.545,
            0.486,
            0.565
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Since ad "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "= b c ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " we can show that"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.46,
            0.568,
            0.536,
            0.599
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_9_equation_15.jpg",
          "content": "d = { \\frac { b c } { a } } ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.616,
            0.835,
            0.675
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Two ratios are proportional if their terms are equal when cross multiplied. The fourth unknown quantity can be found through such cross multiplication."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.686,
            0.848,
            0.78
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In ancient India, Āryabhaṭa (199 CE) and others called such problems of proportionality Rule of Three problems. There were 3 numbers given—the pramāṇa (measure "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "- \\mathbf { a } ^ { \\prime }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " in our case), the phala (fruit — ‘b’ in our case), and the ichchhā (requisition "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "- c"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " in our case). To find the ichchhāphala (yield—‘d’ in our case), Āryabhaṭa says,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.779,
            0.848,
            0.816
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "“Multiply the phala by the ichchhā and divide the resulting product by the pramāṇa.”"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.816,
            0.489,
            0.835
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In other words, Āryabhaṭa says,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.247,
            0.834,
            0.775,
            0.854
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "“pramāṇa : phala :: ichchhā : ichchhāphala,” therefore,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.299,
            0.858,
            0.721,
            0.88
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_9_equation_21.jpg",
          "content": "p r a m { \\bar { a } } n a \\times i c h c h h { \\bar { a } } p h a l a = p h a l a \\times i c h c h h { \\bar { a } } ."
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.078,
            0.914,
            0.128,
            0.938
          ],
          "content": []
        },
        {
